  "number": 6039,
  "title": "Prepare the build for tsdown",
  "body": "> Prepares the build for tsdown; no behavior change in the published packages.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Changed\n\n- 👷🏻 Build checks and tests accept tsdown output as well as tsup, and the CSS placeholder check also finds template literals, in PR [#6039](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6039), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nSome build checks and tests assume today's tsup/esbuild output, so switching to tsdown would fail them, and the `css-inject` check also misses a placeholder written as a template literal. This PR makes them correct for both tools and moves the Lightning CSS options into a shared file; the emitted CSS is byte-identical.\n\n## Design\n\n- The CSS pipeline stays ours (unplugin-lightningcss + `injectCSSPlugin`) rather than `@tsdown/css`, so both bundlers can import `lightningCSSOptions.mjs`. It has one user today; moving it now keeps the tsdown pull request to new configs only.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `vibe-grep` `css-inject.yaml`: also matches template literals (no source writes one today, but `` `@--X--@` `` would survive an unminified build: `injectCSSPlugin` only replaces `\"…\"`)\n- `lightningCSSOptions.mjs`: Lightning CSS options and `removePreserveReason()`, used by `esbuildPlugins.mjs`\n- `api/src/boot/middleware.ts`: `type` on the `AvatarPolymiddlewareProxyProps` re-export\n- `vibe-grep` `lightning-css.yaml`: accepts `:has( > …)` as well as `:has(> …)`\n- `boot/bundle.html`, `fluentTheme/simple.html`, `preact/fluentTheme/simple.html`: build tool may be `tsup` or `tsdown`\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
